  "signature": {
    "algorithm": "hex(HMAC-SHA256(secret, timestamp \\n seed \\n count \\n offset \\n total \\n body))",
    "note": "A service checks ONE signature and cannot tell which runtime sent the request, so these 64 hex digits are the contract rather than an implementation detail. Before this file the value was pinned in two of the five and the derived seed in one: a port could have computed something else entirely and four suites would still have been green, with the failure surfacing only as 401s in a user's service. Since 0.4.0 the message also carries the batch's place in its column — offset (X-TDC-Offset) and total (X-TDC-Total) — so a captured batch cannot be replayed as another one.",
